      "id": "P1",
      "text": "COLONOSCOPY REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 2, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Attending endoscopist: Rafael Duquesne, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Fellow: Mina Halvorsen, MD (fictional), gastroenterology fellow"
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "History: In March 2024 Dr. Corwin Platt (fictional) performed a colonoscopy elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "At that procedure Dr. Platt (fictional) removed a 4 mm rectal polyp with hot biopsy forceps."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "Procedure: The fellow advanced the colonoscope to the cecum under my direct supervision."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "The fellow removed a 7 mm descending colon polyp with a cold snare under my direct supervision."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "I took random cold forceps biopsies of the right and left colon for microscopic colitis."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "- Descending colon: 7 mm sessile polyp, removed with a cold snare as above and retrieved."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "- Colonic mucosa normal throughout; random biopsies taken from the right and left colon."
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "text": "- Rectum: normal, with no residual polyp at the site treated in March 2024."
    },
    {
      "id": "P13",
      "text": "1. 7 mm descending colon polyp, removed by cold snare."
    },
    {
      "id": "P14",
      "text": "2. Normal-appearing colonic mucosa; random biopsies taken to evaluate for microscopic colitis."
    }
  ],
